(46124, 771, 933, '<td valign="top">Very sweet!  Beatiful shot.  Probably my favorite in this cometition.  Only thing keeping me from giving it a 10 are the little black dots just above and to the right of the subject.  I know, I know, kinda picky of me.  But they are just big enough to be noticible, and therefor distracting.  All in all though, excellent work!</td>', 'Very sweet!  Beatiful shot.  Probably my favorite in this cometition.  Only thing keeping me from giving it a 10 are the little black dots just above and to the right of the subject.  I know, I know, kinda picky of me.  But they are just big enough to be noticible, and therefor distracting.  All in all though, excellent work!', '2002-04-12 15:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46125, 771, 428, '<td valign="top">nice depiction of the theme, nice colors. Curious how you set this up? is that a reflection of two or are there actually 4?  Good shot!</td>', 'nice depiction of the theme, nice colors. Curious how you set this up? is that a reflection of two or are there actually 4?  Good shot!', '2002-04-12 17:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46126, 771, 2, '<td valign="top">The intense lighting of this photograph really throws you off -- same with the odd shape.  Nice effect.</td>', 'The intense lighting of this photograph really throws you off -- same with the odd shape.  Nice effect.', '2002-04-13 14:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46127, 771, 739, '<td valign="top">The arrangement of these "french curve" jigs with the orange backround works very well!  Very creative.</td>', 'The arrangement of these "french curve" jigs with the orange backround works very well!  Very creative.', '2002-04-13 15:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46128, 771, 1030, '<td valign="top">I like the composition and the use of the gels on the light.</td>', 'I like the composition and the use of the gels on the light.', '2002-04-13 22:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46129, 771, 637, '<td valign="top">The best. No contest.</td>', 'The best. No contest.', '2002-04-13 23:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46130, 771, 1, '<td valign="top">Great lighting and colors.  Well done.</td>', 'Great lighting and colors.  Well done.', '2002-04-14 11:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46131, 771, 734, '<td valign="top">I love the lighting, but I wonder what it would have looked like with no flash and a long exposure with some softer lighting.<br/></td>', 'I love the lighting, but I wonder what it would have looked like with no flash and a long exposure with some softer lighting.', '2002-04-14 13:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46132, 771, 902, '<td valign="top">Nice use of common objects with just the right lighting</td>', 'Nice use of common objects with just the right lighting', '2002-04-14 19:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46133, 771, 308, '<td valign="top">These colors are superb.</td>', 'These colors are superb.', '2002-04-14 20:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46134, 771, 955, '<td valign="top">superb composition, lighting and colour - excellent</td>', 'superb composition, lighting and colour - excellent', '2002-04-14 21:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46135, 771, 661, '<td valign="top">Interesting lighting and curves.  Nice Composition.</td>', 'Interesting lighting and curves.  Nice Composition.', '2002-04-14 22:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46136, 771, 554, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all. I appreciate your comments.<br/>I will try to answer your questions:  There are two transparent french curves, the smaller one stuck through the larger one. They are setting on what WAS a clean mirror which is laying beside a wall which is Spanish textured and painted a creeme or off white color. The room''s lights were off. The lighting was by "playing" a flashlight onto the curves in a tight circular motion from above. The final result was created by adjusting the global levels. I didn''t notice the speck which shows up as two until the next day when looking at the shots in  ''Elements. I tryed to redo the shot about 60 or so times but was unsuccessful.  Lesson learned------keep an eye on the details BEFORE you make the shot. You might not get the same chance again.  Thanks again for your votes and your comments.   David</td>', 'Thanks to all. I appreciate your comments.I will try to answer your questions:  There are two transparent french curves, the smaller one stuck through the larger one. They are setting on what WAS a clean mirror which is laying beside a wall which is Spanish textured and painted a creeme or off white color. The room''s lights were off. The lighting was by "playing" a flashlight onto the curves in a tight circular motion from above. The final result was created by adjusting the global levels. I didn''t notice the speck which shows up as two until the next day when looking at the shots in  ''Elements. I tryed to redo the shot about 60 or so times but was unsuccessful.  Lesson learned------keep an eye on the details BEFORE you make the shot. You might not get the same chance again.  Thanks again for your votes and your comments.   David', '2002-04-15 20:52:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46137, 772, 789, '<td valign="top">I love Yosimite!!!! Nice photo.</td>', 'I love Yosimite!!!! Nice photo.', '2002-04-08 01:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
