(46703, 796, 1, '<td valign="top">I said bite your tongue because you were obviously misinformed when you made your idiotic comment.<br/><br/>Need I remind you that the point of making comments is for providing constructive feedback for the users in our community, not to let users know that, in your opinion, they don''t have a clue about photography.</td>', 'I said bite your tongue because you were obviously misinformed when you made your idiotic comment.Need I remind you that the point of making comments is for providing constructive feedback for the users in our community, not to let users know that, in your opinion, they don''t have a clue about photography.', '2002-04-15 15:53:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46704, 796, 131, '<td valign="top">Better ways to take a picture of pubic hair - by langdon.<br/><br/>1.  Add hair spray.<br/>2.  Dip in milk<br/>3.  if you run out, ask your mom for some of her''s<br/><br/>my point is.  there is nothing good about this pathetic picture.  There is no way to make it better. Is it really a good idea?  If it''s such a great idea why don''t we make it a topic for everyone.  Instead of a self portrait, why don''t we call it "PUBES"  the curlier the better.  The problem is, no one here has any sense of reality.  This is a photography contest.  Trash really isn''t accepted here, or maybe I''m wrong, obviously no one that runs this site was SMART enough to disqualify this stupid pathetic so called picture.  It is very obvious that the person who took this is immature.  It is very obvious that the person who took this has no class and really is not suitable to be in this type of a contest.  If you''re asking me for a constructive comment,  good luck because I don''t have one !!!!!!</td>', 'Better ways to take a picture of pubic hair - by langdon.1.  Add hair spray.2.  Dip in milk3.  if you run out, ask your mom for some of her''smy point is.  there is nothing good about this pathetic picture.  There is no way to make it better. Is it really a good idea?  If it''s such a great idea why don''t we make it a topic for everyone.  Instead of a self portrait, why don''t we call it "PUBES"  the curlier the better.  The problem is, no one here has any sense of reality.  This is a photography contest.  Trash really isn''t accepted here, or maybe I''m wrong, obviously no one that runs this site was SMART enough to disqualify this stupid pathetic so called picture.  It is very obvious that the person who took this is immature.  It is very obvious that the person who took this has no class and really is not suitable to be in this type of a contest.  If you''re asking me for a constructive comment,  good luck because I don''t have one !!!!!!', '2002-04-15 18:31:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46705, 796, 245, '<td valign="top">Man, langdon is a fierce webmaster!&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;I also think ryano gets much lower votes than he deserves because people (in general) are too uptight. I mean, come on... it''s just a toilet! Toilets get pubic hairs on them. Should we all just pretend that toilets are sparkling temples of hygene?&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;I found the last two of his photographs quite interesting, he actually *has* a visual style, and is not just snapping at random. Frankly, I look forward to seeing what he''s going to submit next. A lot of my favorite artwork makes me flinch... isn''t ''art'' more about a person''s visceral reaction to it than any post-viewing, intellectual, subjective evaluation of it''s ''beauty'' or ''merit''?&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;To those of you who''re demanding that he leaves... not everyone sees the world like you do, I''d appreciate you toning down the vitriol. And to max, the proud owner of our first ''FAGGOT'' comment, if the thought of a guy being close enough to another guy''s pubes to photograph them, even an unattached one, is enough to get you so hot and bothered... wow. I hope the pubes at your workplace don''t turn *you* gay. Better check under the seats.</td>', 'Man, langdon is a fierce webmaster!&lt;/p&gt;I also think ryano gets much lower votes than he deserves because people (in general) are too uptight. I mean, come on... it''s just a toilet! Toilets get pubic hairs on them. Should we all just pretend that toilets are sparkling temples of hygene?&lt;/p&gt;I found the last two of his photographs quite interesting, he actually *has* a visual style, and is not just snapping at random. Frankly, I look forward to seeing what he''s going to submit next. A lot of my favorite artwork makes me flinch... isn''t ''art'' more about a person''s visceral reaction to it than any post-viewing, intellectual, subjective evaluation of it''s ''beauty'' or ''merit''?&lt;/p&gt;To those of you who''re demanding that he leaves... not everyone sees the world like you do, I''d appreciate you toning down the vitriol. And to max, the proud owner of our first ''FAGGOT'' comment, if the thought of a guy being close enough to another guy''s pubes to photograph them, even an unattached one, is enough to get you so hot and bothered... wow. I hope the pubes at your workplace don''t turn *you* gay. Better check under the seats.', '2002-04-16 06:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46706, 796, 1, '<td valign="top">ciscocali, I''m glad you could come with a more idiotic response than your previous.<br/><br/>Either way, there is a lot good about this picture.  It''s real, it''s raw, and causes many different reactions as seen from the various comments.  It''s obviously sparked something in you.  Who says art can''t be controversial?</td>', 'ciscocali, I''m glad you could come with a more idiotic response than your previous.Either way, there is a lot good about this picture.  It''s real, it''s raw, and causes many different reactions as seen from the various comments.  It''s obviously sparked something in you.  Who says art can''t be controversial?', '2002-04-16 06:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46707, 796, 245, '<td valign="top">You know, I should have addressed ciscocali directly. For someone who speaks so strongly of class and taste, you sure don''t hold back on the tactless attacks on everyone who doesn''t agree with you. Why, it took you a mere four sentences to go from insulting rynao, to insulting professor, to insulting all us clueless tools who don''t know what photography ''stands for'' today. Why don''t you tell us? I''m so happy that I''ve finally met the arbiter of all things digital, now I have someone to answer my burning questions about photgraphic propriety and the online social graces. And shame on you for criticizing professor for not submitting, as if that were a reason he couldn''t comment inteligently. Where are your Curves and Stopped Motion pictures?  I really did like your architecture submission, back it up with another submission or pipe down.</td>', 'You know, I should have addressed ciscocali directly. For someone who speaks so strongly of class and taste, you sure don''t hold back on the tactless attacks on everyone who doesn''t agree with you. Why, it took you a mere four sentences to go from insulting rynao, to insulting professor, to insulting all us clueless tools who don''t know what photography ''stands for'' today. Why don''t you tell us? I''m so happy that I''ve finally met the arbiter of all things digital, now I have someone to answer my burning questions about photgraphic propriety and the online social graces. And shame on you for criticizing professor for not submitting, as if that were a reason he couldn''t comment inteligently. Where are your Curves and Stopped Motion pictures?  I really did like your architecture submission, back it up with another submission or pipe down.', '2002-04-16 06:39:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46708, 796, 437, '<td valign="top">to my dear friend ciscocali, <br/><br/>yes i am just a voter and a professor.  i vote on pictures here in the same way i grade my student''s homework--with a keen eye and complete impartiality.  i do not have time to photograph just like i''m sure you do not have time to write textbooks on the human psyche.  we both do what we do and who is to judge that a photographer is better than a voter.  is an athelete better than a judge?  the judge has the final say.  we all know that if an athlete felt his pride was hurt in anyway, he would not hesitate to criticize the judge.  your comments were made out of anger which is a perfectly normal reaction of the homo sapien.  it should be brought to your attention that you and your submissions aren''t in anyway needed for the growth and survival of dpchallenge.  i do not think the three gentleman who created this site gave of their time and hard work so you could tell them "Better ways to take a picture of pubic hair".  i hope either an apology, silence, or a simple exit will follow this post.  thanks.</td>', 'to my dear friend ciscocali, yes i am just a voter and a professor.  i vote on pictures here in the same way i grade my student''s homework--with a keen eye and complete impartiality.  i do not have time to photograph just like i''m sure you do not have time to write textbooks on the human psyche.  we both do what we do and who is to judge that a photographer is better than a voter.  is an athelete better than a judge?  the judge has the final say.  we all know that if an athlete felt his pride was hurt in anyway, he would not hesitate to criticize the judge.  your comments were made out of anger which is a perfectly normal reaction of the homo sapien.  it should be brought to your attention that you and your submissions aren''t in anyway needed for the growth and survival of dpchallenge.  i do not think the three gentleman who created this site gave of their time and hard work so you could tell them "Better ways to take a picture of pubic hair".  i hope either an apology, silence, or a simple exit will follow this post.  thanks.', '2002-04-16 07:51:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46709, 796, 255, '<td valign="top">Hello Ryano, you controversy-sparking photographer you! Not unlike like my much-loved Mapplethorpe. Good for you for keeping us on our toes! I happen to enjoy your pictures because they are so unpredictable and always make me laugh. I am still laughing about the "location-Mother F***er" on your self portrait--not mention it was a cool picture! Keep ''em coming!</td>', 'Hello Ryano, you controversy-sparking photographer you! Not unlike like my much-loved Mapplethorpe. Good for you for keeping us on our toes! I happen to enjoy your pictures because they are so unpredictable and always make me laugh. I am still laughing about the "location-Mother F***er" on your self portrait--not mention it was a cool picture! Keep ''em coming!', '2002-04-16 20:32:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46710, 796, 671, '<td valign="top">visually uninteresting</td>', 'visually uninteresting', '2002-04-16 22:30:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46711, 796, 1, '<td valign="top">I don''t feel that this photograph is visually uninteresting, at all.  I think that the pubic hair, as grotesque as pubic hairs may be, is very crisp and really stands out in such a dark image.  It''s almost as if I should brush it off my own computer screen.</td>', 'I don''t feel that this photograph is visually uninteresting, at all.  I think that the pubic hair, as grotesque as pubic hairs may be, is very crisp and really stands out in such a dark image.  It''s almost as if I should brush it off my own computer screen.', '2002-04-17 09:39:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46712, 796, 1157, '<td valign="top">NICE</td>', 'NICE', '2002-04-18 12:59:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46713, 796, 933, '<td valign="top">Frankly, I find this and some of ryano''s other images pretty damn humorous in a darkly disturbed kind of way.  Keep up the great work, you pube-shooting psycho!  Without visionary artisitic leaders such as yourselves, the world would be a grey, boring, overly-anal shithole.  VanGough, Picasso, Escher - they too were all misunderstood.  (Oh gawd, did I just unconciously compare "Lone Pubert, ye hardly knew we" to "A Starry Night"?)  LOL!</td>', 'Frankly, I find this and some of ryano''s other images pretty damn humorous in a darkly disturbed kind of way.  Keep up the great work, you pube-shooting psycho!  Without visionary artisitic leaders such as yourselves, the world would be a grey, boring, overly-anal shithole.  VanGough, Picasso, Escher - they too were all misunderstood.  (Oh gawd, did I just unconciously compare "Lone Pubert, ye hardly knew we" to "A Starry Night"?)  LOL!', '2002-04-18 13:36:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46714, 796, 47, '<td valign="top">re:<br/>5) jon sucks<br/><br/>see previous:<br/>max - 4/13/2002<br/>FAGGOT<br/><br/>addendum:<br/>&amp;lt;3</td>', 're:5) jon suckssee previous:max - 4/13/2002FAGGOTaddendum:&lt;3', '2002-04-18 20:57:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46715, 796, 255, '<td valign="top">I think we are looking at the next David Lynch or maybe S. Kubrick.</td>', 'I think we are looking at the next David Lynch or maybe S. Kubrick.', '2002-04-19 01:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(46716, 797, 656, '<td valign="top">Good macro.  Lighting needs some work to be more diffuse.</td>', 'Good macro.  Lighting needs some work to be more diffuse.', '2002-04-08 10:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46717, 797, 509, '<td valign="top">Wow, two of you here have freaky watches</td>', 'Wow, two of you here have freaky watches', '2002-04-08 11:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46718, 797, 772, '<td valign="top">I like the subject of your photograph.  The light glare near the watch dial is a bit too strong.  The photo is a little grainy as well... maybe comes from cropping this segment from a much larger original photograph...</td>', 'I like the subject of your photograph.  The light glare near the watch dial is a bit too strong.  The photo is a little grainy as well... maybe comes from cropping this segment from a much larger original photograph...', '2002-04-08 12:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46719, 797, 279, '<td valign="top">The flash flare at the top ruins what would otherwise be a pretty photo.</td>', 'The flash flare at the top ruins what would otherwise be a pretty photo.', '2002-04-08 13:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46720, 797, 327, '<td valign="top">over compressed or glare? Still not a bad shot.</td>', 'over compressed or glare? Still not a bad shot.', '2002-04-08 20:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46721, 797, 472, '<td valign="top">killer!  too bad about the reflection in the glass of the flash.</td>', 'killer!  too bad about the reflection in the glass of the flash.', '2002-04-08 21:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46722, 797, 244, '<td valign="top">the bright spot on the face of the watch is a little too distracting, along with the grain from the wood.</td>', 'the bright spot on the face of the watch is a little too distracting, along with the grain from the wood.', '2002-04-08 21:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46723, 797, 587, '<td valign="top">Too bad there is so much glare, missing some of the detail because of it. It does seem to be an awesome watch though!</td>', 'Too bad there is so much glare, missing some of the detail because of it. It does seem to be an awesome watch though!', '2002-04-09 06:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46724, 797, 797, '<td valign="top">two watches! like the other one, i don''t quite agree with the bright patch of light.</td>', 'two watches! like the other one, i don''t quite agree with the bright patch of light.', '2002-04-09 08:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46725, 797, 352, '<td valign="top">Nice detail.  The flash spots are a bit distracting.  I''d try to take this picture with more ambient lighting and no flash.  If you can extend your shutter speed (and have a tripod or means of steadying your camera) you could do this under normal lighting</td>', 'Nice detail.  The flash spots are a bit distracting.  I''d try to take this picture with more ambient lighting and no flash.  If you can extend your shutter speed (and have a tripod or means of steadying your camera) you could do this under normal lighting', '2002-04-09 10:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46726, 797, 330, '<td valign="top">Nice shot but the flare at the top is a little annoying. Plus I think it''s more circles than curves</td>', 'Nice shot but the flare at the top is a little annoying. Plus I think it''s more circles than curves', '2002-04-09 11:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46727, 797, 280, '<td valign="top">too many reflections off the glass.</td>', 'too many reflections off the glass.', '2002-04-09 14:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46728, 797, 139, '<td valign="top">Nice watch!</td>', 'Nice watch!', '2002-04-09 17:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46729, 797, 441, '<td valign="top">great detail.</td>', 'great detail.', '2002-04-10 14:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46730, 797, 347, '<td valign="top">It might be just me, but circles don''t make me think "curves". To me, a curve is an open-ended, continuous unbounded thing. Technically, this has to have been a tricky shot; use of macro is good, but the lighting glares on the watch case, hiding some of the detail.</td>', 'It might be just me, but circles don''t make me think "curves". To me, a curve is an open-ended, continuous unbounded thing. Technically, this has to have been a tricky shot; use of macro is good, but the lighting glares on the watch case, hiding some of the detail.', '2002-04-10 15:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46731, 797, 428, '<td valign="top">nice shot, but a little too much flash on the top of the watch</td>', 'nice shot, but a little too much flash on the top of the watch', '2002-04-10 21:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46732, 797, 245, '<td valign="top">The glare is washes out a lot of detail in this photo, and the watch kinda crooked. I''d try using artificial light and try very hard to line the watch perfectly square with the camera, and zoom in enough to lose the knob or out enough to capture the whole thing. :)</td>', 'The glare is washes out a lot of detail in this photo, and the watch kinda crooked. I''d try using artificial light and try very hard to line the watch perfectly square with the camera, and zoom in enough to lose the knob or out enough to capture the whole thing. :)', '2002-04-11 13:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46733, 797, 714, '<td valign="top">The light at the top of the watch is distacting..other then that it is great. :)</td>', 'The light at the top of the watch is distacting..other then that it is great. :)', '2002-04-11 16:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46734, 797, 811, '<td valign="top">a little too bright at the top<br/>nice watch</td>', 'a little too bright at the topnice watch', '2002-04-12 15:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46735, 797, 447, '<td valign="top">The flash marks are distracting.</td>', 'The flash marks are distracting.', '2002-04-12 20:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46736, 797, 2, '<td valign="top">The glare distracts from the image, and you''re slightly off-center.  Maybe a tighter shot with better lighting?</td>', 'The glare distracts from the image, and you''re slightly off-center.  Maybe a tighter shot with better lighting?', '2002-04-13 14:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46737, 797, 739, '<td valign="top">Would have been better without the glare.</td>', 'Would have been better without the glare.', '2002-04-13 15:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46738, 797, 881, '<td valign="top">I think uniform lighting across the watch would have worked better</td>', 'I think uniform lighting across the watch would have worked better', '2002-04-13 23:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46739, 797, 734, '<td valign="top">Great macro, the lens flares are a bit distracting,.. maybe a long exposure with softer lighting.</td>', 'Great macro, the lens flares are a bit distracting,.. maybe a long exposure with softer lighting.', '2002-04-14 13:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46740, 797, 689, '<td valign="top">Try tilting the watch to remove the glare, unless you want to get a polarizing filter.</td>', 'Try tilting the watch to remove the glare, unless you want to get a polarizing filter.', '2002-04-14 16:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46741, 797, 902, '<td valign="top">nice watch too bad there is the light at the top</td>', 'nice watch too bad there is the light at the top', '2002-04-14 19:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46742, 797, 955, '<td valign="top">good impact, lighting and composition</td>', 'good impact, lighting and composition', '2002-04-14 22:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46743, 797, 661, '<td valign="top">Interesting detail.  The glare was distracting.</td>', 'Interesting detail.  The glare was distracting.', '2002-04-14 22:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46744, 798, 270, '<td valign="top">A better surface/backdrop for the watch would make this much nicer.</td>', 'A better surface/backdrop for the watch would make this much nicer.', '2002-04-08 01:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46745, 798, 51, '<td valign="top">somewhat blurry. lackluster composition.</td>', 'somewhat blurry. lackluster composition.', '2002-04-08 09:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46746, 798, 656, '<td valign="top">Need to work on the focus/ sharpness</td>', 'Need to work on the focus/ sharpness', '2002-04-08 10:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46747, 798, 772, '<td valign="top">This is very similar to another photo in the challenge.  I like the subject but this photo has the same distracting feature as the other one like it... the glare is a little rough....</td>', 'This is very similar to another photo in the challenge.  I like the subject but this photo has the same distracting feature as the other one like it... the glare is a little rough....', '2002-04-08 13:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46748, 798, 749, '<td valign="top">If the light more central, the detail would appear more balanced.</td>', 'If the light more central, the detail would appear more balanced.', '2002-04-08 16:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46749, 798, 279, '<td valign="top">Flash flare just ruins it.</td>', 'Flash flare just ruins it.', '2002-04-08 17:12:00.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(46750, 798, 714, '<td valign="top">To much light.  Maybe if you shut the flash off and had the watch in a well lit room, the light would have been more evenly distributed on the watch.  I like your idea.  :)</td>', 'To much light.  Maybe if you shut the flash off and had the watch in a well lit room, the light would have been more evenly distributed on the watch.  I like your idea.  :)', '2002-04-08 17:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46751, 798, 441, '<td valign="top">nice closeup - soft focus?</td>', 'nice closeup - soft focus?', '2002-04-08 17:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46752, 798, 641, '<td valign="top">Nice, would have like to see it even closer with less background area.</td>', 'Nice, would have like to see it even closer with less background area.', '2002-04-09 08:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46753, 798, 797, '<td valign="top">nice idea. i would''ve preferred a uniformly dark background, though. the patch of white in the upper right doesn''t work for me.</td>', 'nice idea. i would''ve preferred a uniformly dark background, though. the patch of white in the upper right doesn''t work for me.', '2002-04-09 08:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46754, 798, 472, '<td valign="top">great watch,  focus is hard for macros. i would have focussed a little better.</td>', 'great watch,  focus is hard for macros. i would have focussed a little better.', '2002-04-09 12:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46755, 798, 509, '<td valign="top">Would have looked nicer centerred I think.  Lighting is a bit harsh, but is necessary to make the watch shine.  Overally a good photo.</td>', 'Would have looked nicer centerred I think.  Lighting is a bit harsh, but is necessary to make the watch shine.  Overally a good photo.', '2002-04-09 13:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46756, 798, 884, '<td valign="top">Interesting. Clever idea.</td>', 'Interesting. Clever idea.', '2002-04-09 14:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46757, 798, 139, '<td valign="top">What a great watch!</td>', 'What a great watch!', '2002-04-09 17:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46758, 798, 245, '<td valign="top">Soft focus and blown out hilights take a a lot away from this. Did you sharpen it? It''s also cropped more on the top than on the bottom.</td>', 'Soft focus and blown out hilights take a a lot away from this. Did you sharpen it? It''s also cropped more on the top than on the bottom.', '2002-04-10 13:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46759, 798, 347, '<td valign="top">Other than the watch case, there really are hardly any obvious curves here. You''ve managed to avoid reflections to a great degree, but the lighting is still too directional for such a finely detailed subject -- try more indirect lighting for this, IMHO.</td>', 'Other than the watch case, there really are hardly any obvious curves here. You''ve managed to avoid reflections to a great degree, but the lighting is still too directional for such a finely detailed subject -- try more indirect lighting for this, IMHO.', '2002-04-10 15:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46760, 798, 131, '<td valign="top">nothing special</td>', 'nothing special', '2002-04-10 19:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46761, 798, 811, '<td valign="top">good detail, but a little bright on the right side</td>', 'good detail, but a little bright on the right side', '2002-04-12 15:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46762, 798, 352, '<td valign="top">Your flash created a hot spot in teh upper right hand cornere. Perhaps a stnad, tripod, or something and a longer shutter speed would have helped here.</td>', 'Your flash created a hot spot in teh upper right hand cornere. Perhaps a stnad, tripod, or something and a longer shutter speed would have helped here.', '2002-04-12 20:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46763, 798, 689, '<td valign="top">Watch your framing ... you cut off the top of the watch, plus your light source is a bit hot on the upper right.</td>', 'Watch your framing ... you cut off the top of the watch, plus your light source is a bit hot on the upper right.', '2002-04-14 16:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(46764, 798, 661, '<td valign="top">A beautiful watch but the glare is distracting.</td>', 'A beautiful watch but the glare is distracting.', '2002-04-14 23:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(177990, 715, 1003, '<td valign="top">i think maybe, i would have cropped a little off the top.....</td>', 'i think maybe, i would have cropped a little off the top.....', '2002-12-25 09:22:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(367003, 724, 327, '<td valign="top">I love the lighting on these bananas. Beautiful shot.</td>', 'I love the lighting on these bananas. Beautiful shot.', '2003-07-25 18:18:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(447891, 771, 12223, '<td valign="top">I really like this photograph.  Particularly the color, then the asthetics of the shapes.  I find this quite original.  Nice eye. My only distraction is the printing on the curves.</td>', 'I really like this photograph.  Particularly the color, then the asthetics of the shapes.  I find this quite original.  Nice eye. My only distraction is the printing on the curves.', '2003-10-12 19:03:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(454720, 771, 9441, '<td valign="top">Very cool!  Wonderful color, terrific clarity...good job!</td>', 'Very cool!  Wonderful color, terrific clarity...good job!', '2003-10-18 16:31:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(704927, 771, 8860, '<td valign="top">Nice subject (reminds me of the manual days of design!). Composition would benefit from ofsetting the subject to bottom right, creating some lead-in lines. Arranging the French Curves less rigidly would enhance the aesthetics too.</td>', 'Nice subject (reminds me of the manual days of design!). Composition would benefit from ofsetting the subject to bottom right, creating some lead-in lines. Arranging the French Curves less rigidly would enhance the aesthetics too.', '2004-05-07 21:36:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(761051, 650, 22734, '<td valign="top">Very nice image</td>', 'Very nice image', '2004-06-13 00:25:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(850239, 759, 18084, '<td valign="top">I read the tutorial and did it...it turned out very cool! Thanxxxxx</td>', 'I read the tutorial and did it...it turned out very cool! Thanxxxxx', '2004-08-09 03:37:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(892196, 771, 22734, '<td valign="top">I love this composition. It is truly beautiful. Even as is, I am placing it in my favorites. I look at images and when I work I do so in series. That is, I vary the lighting and then look and see what else can I do to improve it. I love the transition from yellow to red and would have prefered a slower transition between the white and the yellow. Of course, it is easy to point out ideas and changes once a concept is born. Here I concede that your concept is indeed above average. It has a flair and beauty to boot.</td>', 'I love this composition. It is truly beautiful. Even as is, I am placing it in my favorites. I look at images and when I work I do so in series. That is, I vary the lighting and then look and see what else can I do to improve it. I love the transition from yellow to red and would have prefered a slower transition between the white and the yellow. Of course, it is easy to point out ideas and changes once a concept is born. Here I concede that your concept is indeed above average. It has a flair and beauty to boot.', '2004-09-04 01:00:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(892877, 730, 23620, '<td valign="top"><b>BOLDring</b></td>', 'BOLDring', '2004-09-04 16:41:35.000000', NULL, 0),
